<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 15 November, from 1315 to 1920.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/austria" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1315 <span class="tih-ago">711 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Swiss confederates ambush the Habsburgs at Morgarten</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Men of Schwyz, Uri and Unterwalden ambushed Duke Leopold of Austria's army on a narrow path by Lake Ägeri. The victory strengthened the young Swiss Confederation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1777 <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress adopts the Articles of Confederation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Continental Congress approved the Articles of Confederation, the first constitution of the United States. Ratified in 1781, they gave the central government too little power and were replaced in 1789.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1864 <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sherman leaves Atlanta on his March to the Sea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After burning much of Atlanta, William T. Sherman's army set off for Savannah. Its destruction of railways, crops and property across Georgia aimed to break the Confederacy's capacity and will to fight.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1889 <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A military coup makes Brazil a republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marshal Deodoro da Fonseca led a coup in Rio de Janeiro that deposed Emperor Pedro II and proclaimed the Republic of Brazil. The 64-year-old emperor went into exile in Europe.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca">Deodoro da Fonseca</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/league-of-nations.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1920 <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The League of Nations holds its first Assembly</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 41 nations met in Geneva for the first Assembly of the League of Nations. Weakened by the absence of the United States, the League failed to prevent the aggression of the 1930s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
